{"author":{"id":"609bf866d4a5d716c19faf5d617b3bf3de478230d29602d72aad5aa90a80466f"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1791628565,"nonce":"GraKOd4Pbi9PhmSGVAK9WPXtyzc=","message":"Fixed on branch perf-queue (not on main yet) by 7ad3b4149f77e432ec4b218a8f08e2147b0153d5 and 56602efe17e650f80a8f33c795b63ba18addd85d, with two more that came out of the same trace: 2dd3202fd4bb2a428e684ab17624a17b899546b7 (an f32 register at an OSR entry, ceb2a47) and 9cf6e8ec0746bccc901bad291b3bb9adaae418ea (the re-tier sites' analysis cost, 3991836).\n\nThree things kept findex 869 in the interpreter, in this order.\n\n1. osr::analyze refused the whole function for one loop's hazard and refused every loop a Ref's block could reach. It now refuses loop by loop, and only a pointer that is stored, returned or merged by a phi is a hazard: HL gives a Ref no life beyond the call it is passed to, so the entries point such a pointer at their own cell (Cranelift: stack_addr of the entry's slot; LLVM: the entry's alloca) instead of loading the interpreter's address.\n2. The Cranelift entry declined an inner loop whose outer loop defines a value the inner loop reads (\"used before its in-region definition\"), which is every nested loop whose outer body makes a local. Such a value is now a Variable: the buffer's value on the first pass, the outer body's on later ones, and the frontend places the phis. Dominance is computed over the entry's own region.\n3. Any f32 register in the function declined the Cranelift entry.\n\nResults. The committed reproducer bytecode (control build, --preset game, same checksum 101682.393993095 throughout), Mac:\n\n    hybrid       24-25 s wall -\u003e 5 s wall   (loadMs 573 ms)\n    --mode jit   4 s\n    findex 869   enters compiled code at pc=1345\n\nChimpMonk's rig-binding and humanoid checks pass, 10 s -\u003e 6 s. Functions an OSR entry can be built for (ASH_VERIFY_OSR=only): the glTF program 636 -\u003e 728 of 742, ChimpMonk's checks 1001 -\u003e 1170 of 1222.\n\nNUC benchmark sweeps (scripts/ash_bench.py, 3d5ab48 as --ash-base interleaved, 9 to 15 timed runs, answers checked), hybrid-auto: mandelbrot_small 313-527 ms -\u003e 16-34 ms (-91..-93%, every one of its loops was refused for RefTaken), binary_trees -23..-32%, simd_dot -10..-35%, array_push -18%; nothing slower outside the base's own spread (deltablue, which is bimodal, is +0.4% over 30 runs).\n\nGates: unit conformance 1069/1069 on interp, hybrid, jit and aot (Mac); ash_core 94, air 205, ash_interp 7 unit tests; osr_retier (new fixtures for refs before a loop, f32, nested loops), ref_args, f32_tier_parity, retyped_reads, fma_promotion_parity, parity_matrix, stdlib_matrix, llvm_worker_pool, wide_hybrid pass; the new fixtures give the interpreter's answers on the NUC as well. osr_retier's forced_snapshots test is the open 316cce8 and fails on the Mac with and without these commits.\n\nStill open from the profile: MultipleLatches (a while loop with `continue`) is still refused loop by loop; four of this function's loops were that.","files":null}]}